<section class="size-guide-page" aria-label="Size guide">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sizing-tip">
      <strong>How to measure your ring size:</strong> Wrap a strip of paper snugly around the base of your finger, mark where it overlaps, then measure the length in millimetres against a ruler. Compare that measurement with the <em>inner circumference</em> column below. For the most accurate result, measure at the end of the day when fingers are at their largest.
    </div>

    <div class="size-guide-grid">
      <div>
        <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: 1.35rem;">Ring Size Chart</h2>
        <table class="ring-size-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>US / Canada</th>
              <th>UK / AU</th>
              <th>Circumference (mm)</th>
              <th>Diameter (mm)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% ringSizes.forEach(size => { %>
              <tr>
                <td><%= size.us %></td>
                <td><%= size.uk %></td>
                <td><%= size.circumference %></td>
                <td><%= size.diameter %></td>
              </tr>
            <% }) %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: 1.35rem;">Measuring Tips</h2>
        <div class="sizing-tip">
          <strong>Do's:</strong> Measure your finger at room temperature, on the finger you'll wear the ring, and with the ring passing comfortably over the knuckle. A well-fitting ring spins freely but needs a gentle tug to come off.
        </div>
        <div class="sizing-tip">
          <strong>Don'ts:</strong> Don't measure early in the morning or after exercise, when fingers are smaller. Don't use a sewing tape alone — the paper-strip method is far more accurate. And don't estimate from an existing ring without checking its inner diameter against the chart.
        </div>
        <div class="sizing-tip">
          <strong>Bracelets &amp; necklaces:</strong> Bracelets generally measure by wrist circumference plus 1&ndash;1.5 cm of ease. Necklaces: a 16&nbsp;in choker sits at the collarbone, 18&nbsp;in falls to the collarbone, 20&nbsp;in reaches the décolletage, and 24&nbsp;in hangs to the sternum.
        </div>
        <p class="section-subtitle" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Still unsure? <a href="/contact" class="section-link" style="color: var(--color-gold);">Contact our concierge</a> — we'll help you find the perfect size.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>